{"name":"logicore-code/moongrad","readme":"README.md","yanked":false,"license":"Apache-2.0","version":"0.9.0","checksum":"cb342091beeda3c47660d08d0a70db81c225f16bec04c07b3f3e2787b5cfab8a","keywords":["automatic-differentiation","gradient","hessian","machine-learning","compiler","differentiable-programming","numerical-computing","tensor","wasm","moonbit"],"created_at":"2026-11-27T14:37:33.123241+00:00","repository":"https://github.com/logicore-code/moongrad","description":"Reverse-mode automatic differentiation for MoonBit. The forward pass is constant propagation over a hash-consed DAG; the backward pass is a symbolic compiler that emits a gradient program rather than accumulating adjoints. The program can be re-evaluated at any input and differentiated again, so the same machinery gives second derivatives and second-order optimisation. Includes multi-dimensional tensors with broadcasting, convolution, normalisation layers, mini-batch training, a choice of optimisers and schedules, dense linear algebra with Krylov solvers, and Hessian-vector products.","yanked_reason":null,"preferred-target":"wasm","supported-targets":"+wasm+wasm-gc+js+native"}
